00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:30.080
Thank you.

00:30:00.090 --> 00:30:00.410
Oh

00:30:32.010 --> 00:30:32.330
Thank you.

00:31:06.170 --> 00:31:08.690
Pinwheel spinning around

00:31:08.690 --> 00:31:12.660
Look through my pinwheel and see what I found

00:31:12.660 --> 00:31:16.060
Pinwheel, pinwheel, where have you been?

00:31:17.280 --> 00:31:23.730
How are you? I may have come in

00:31:25.870 --> 00:31:29.660
Pinwheel, pinwheel spinning around

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:32.880
Look to my tinderland, see what I found.

00:31:33.560 --> 00:31:36.560
Tandwheels, then look breezy and bright.

00:31:37.080 --> 00:31:39.980
Then make good morning and then make good night.

00:31:48.190 --> 00:31:51.880
Okay, Silas, are you ready for your harmonica lesson?

00:31:52.420 --> 00:31:53.860
I'm ready, maestro.

00:31:54.420 --> 00:31:59.350
I've been practicing on this here harmonica all week.

00:32:00.120 --> 00:32:06.620
Good, good. You know, Silas, my friend, the harmonica is one of my favorite musical instruments.

00:32:06.840 --> 00:32:07.620
So they tell me.

00:32:07.760 --> 00:32:11.970
It brings tears to my eyes every time I hear it played.

00:32:13.160 --> 00:32:15.290
So, Silas, now's your chance.

00:32:16.270 --> 00:32:17.610
Play your harmonica!

00:32:27.780 --> 00:32:29.980
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no!

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:31.440
No, you're playing it all wrong!

00:32:32.260 --> 00:32:33.240
I know.

00:32:33.900 --> 00:32:35.400
I was playing it.

00:32:35.560 --> 00:32:36.900
Too slowly.

00:32:38.310 --> 00:32:42.730
I usually do things too slowly for everybody.

00:32:43.500 --> 00:32:43.820
Hey.

00:32:44.230 --> 00:32:45.530
No side of that.

00:32:47.900 --> 00:32:48.740
Me?

00:32:49.060 --> 00:32:49.580
Fat?

00:32:50.380 --> 00:32:50.740
Yes.

00:32:51.270 --> 00:32:51.610
You.

00:32:51.890 --> 00:32:52.050
What?

00:32:52.200 --> 00:32:57.780
Wow, this is the first time in my whole life that I've ever done anything fast.

00:32:58.340 --> 00:32:59.800
Listen to me, Silas.

00:33:00.120 --> 00:33:01.440
Music is not a race!

00:33:02.200 --> 00:33:04.580
Here, just follow my beat.

00:33:04.920 --> 00:33:06.760
Me. Fast.

00:33:08.500 --> 00:33:09.800
Watch my baton.

00:33:10.270 --> 00:33:10.730
Good time.

00:33:18.620 --> 00:33:18.920
Good idea.

00:33:19.350 --> 00:33:21.090
I see what you mean.

00:33:21.330 --> 00:33:21.910
Try it again.

00:33:22.150 --> 00:33:22.510
Okay.

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:31.640
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:33:33.920 --> 00:33:37.040
You do know what slow means, don't you?

00:33:37.720 --> 00:33:41.200
I sure do, but I don't know what comes over me.

00:33:41.300 --> 00:33:45.180
When I play the harmonica, I get so excited.

00:33:46.180 --> 00:33:47.300
Okay, okay, okay, okay, okay, Tyler.

00:33:47.760 --> 00:33:50.400
But let's try it one more time with feeling.

00:33:51.040 --> 00:33:51.300
What?

00:33:51.580 --> 00:33:52.200
Shall we begin?

00:33:52.380 --> 00:33:53.540
More with feeling.

00:33:54.290 --> 00:33:56.330
And a wha...

00:33:57.340 --> 00:33:58.940
A wha...

00:33:59.190 --> 00:33:59.970
And a...

00:34:17.680 --> 00:34:23.280
I can't believe it! At last! Someone in the world can't keep up with me!

00:34:35.400 --> 00:34:40.060
Something comes over me when I play the harmonica, don't you know?

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:00.640
Let's go.

00:35:22.360 --> 00:35:23.560
Simon was enjoying himself.

00:35:23.900 --> 00:35:25.040
drawing on his blackboard.

00:35:25.590 --> 00:35:26.330
But he had to stop.

00:35:26.840 --> 00:35:28.080
It was time for his music listening.

00:35:29.500 --> 00:35:30.000
On his way.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:32.860
Simon met Henry, his chalk drawing friend.

00:35:34.010 --> 00:35:37.720
Simon, someone very sad needs cheering up. Can you help?

00:35:38.660 --> 00:35:41.140
Simon was happy to go with Henry to the land of chalk drawings.

00:35:41.960 --> 00:35:48.230
And they arrived. Henry led him to the wood.

00:35:49.570 --> 00:35:52.530
Simon could hear some very loud sobbing and crying.

00:35:53.840 --> 00:35:59.220
And there, in the darkest shadows, was the elephant looking the picture of misery.

00:36:00.250 --> 00:36:02.200
Dear me, whatever's the matter?

00:36:03.080 --> 00:36:07.280
The elephant managed to stop crying and asked Simon to listen to something.

00:36:10.950 --> 00:36:14.620
There, you hear that? That's what's making me so miserable.

00:36:16.020 --> 00:36:20.210
You see, I want to be musical, but I only blow one note.

00:36:24.620 --> 00:36:25.720
The birds sing.

00:36:31.020 --> 00:36:53.000
the soldiers play instruments the guy can make is one note you see everyone laughs

00:37:06.260 --> 00:37:21.480
what did I tell you I do so want to be musical Simon felt very sorry for the

00:37:21.480 --> 00:37:28.020
elephant then he had an idea he took out his chalk and changed the elephant's

00:37:28.020 --> 00:37:29.340
trunk into a saxophone.

00:37:30.440 --> 00:37:32.820
And now the elephant could play whatever notes he liked.

00:37:36.800 --> 00:37:39.880
Simon headed for home, pleased that he'd been able to help.

00:37:40.480 --> 00:37:44.050
The birds were singing, the band was playing, everyone was happy.

00:37:45.850 --> 00:37:49.750
Suddenly, there was the deafening noise of a giant saxophone.

00:37:51.240 --> 00:37:53.820
Everyone was startled and ran away with their hands over their ears.

00:37:54.920 --> 00:37:58.280
The elephant was enjoying himself so much, he didn't notice how upset everyone was.

00:38:00.670 --> 00:38:06.960
On and on he marched round the land of chalk drawings, and on and on went the deafening saxophone music.

00:38:08.500 --> 00:38:13.060
Simon and the people were at a loss for long.

00:38:13.890 --> 00:38:17.730
The elephant began to get tired and hot and hungry and thirsty.

00:38:19.420 --> 00:38:20.920
Then the elephant found he had a problem.

00:38:22.440 --> 00:38:28.570
As he had no trunk, only a saxophone, he couldn't drink, he couldn't eat either.

00:38:31.950 --> 00:38:38.000
The elephant became miserable again, more miserable than before, and he couldn't even blow his trunk.

00:38:43.460 --> 00:38:44.380
He went up to Simon.

00:38:45.440 --> 00:38:50.920
Simon, I can play music, all right, but I can't eat or drink. I shall starve if you don't do something.

00:38:54.160 --> 00:38:58.390
So Simon changed the saxophone back into an elephant's trunk again.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:01.100
And Simon had another idea.

00:39:01.880 --> 00:39:05.460
He talked with the band leader who gave the elephant some written music.

00:39:07.210 --> 00:39:12.400
The music had one note for the elephant to play, which fitted in perfectly with the band music.

00:39:13.800 --> 00:39:16.220
The elephant was musical, after all.

00:39:17.240 --> 00:39:20.120
And now, while Simon left to go to his own music lesson,

00:39:20.590 --> 00:39:23.290
the chalk drawing people, instead of laughing at the elephant,

00:39:23.850 --> 00:39:28.150
clapped and cheered as he played real music with the chalk drawing band.

00:40:04.700 --> 00:40:16.880
in a beautiful field full of wild flowers lived a very happy little cricket she danced all day and

00:40:16.880 --> 00:40:22.500
played on the fiddle from the first rays of sunshine in the day until way into the night

00:40:22.500 --> 00:40:28.370
she played her fiddle and entertained the other animals with their pretty songs it was like that

00:40:28.370 --> 00:40:29.880
in the spring it was

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:37.790
like that in the summer. Even in the fall, when the ant, who lived on the edge of the forest,

00:40:38.050 --> 00:40:45.820
was gathering food for the winter, the cricket continued to play her fiddle. Fiddly dee, fiddly

00:40:45.820 --> 00:40:56.850
da, fiddly dum. But soon the winter came with snow and frost and howling winds. The ant and all

00:40:56.850 --> 00:40:59.640
the other animals crept deeper into their nests.

00:41:00.060 --> 00:41:02.300
and ate the food they had gathered through the fall.

00:41:02.870 --> 00:41:05.450
But the cricket, who had played all during the fall,

00:41:05.630 --> 00:41:09.450
and did not collect anything, was very hungry.

00:41:10.500 --> 00:41:14.040
She was cold, too, for she had not fixed her house for the winter,

00:41:14.340 --> 00:41:16.280
and had danced and played instead.

00:41:16.400 --> 00:41:21.430
But then the cricket remembered how the other animals enjoyed listening to her that summer,

00:41:22.100 --> 00:41:23.020
especially the ant.

00:41:24.070 --> 00:41:27.190
And so the cricket decided to go to the ant to ask for help.

00:41:28.320 --> 00:41:29.980
I'm very hungry, she said.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:34.770
said, would you please give me something to eat? I will gather some food and I promise

00:41:34.770 --> 00:41:40.940
that I will repay you next summer. But the aunt did not want to give anything to the

00:41:40.940 --> 00:41:47.540
cricket. She only asked her, hmm, what did you do all summer long? As though she could

00:41:47.540 --> 00:41:53.640
not remember. You know what I did, answered the cricket. I danced and played with my fiddle.

00:41:53.880 --> 00:41:59.740
I completely forgot all about the winter coming. So you forgot, did you?

00:42:00.060 --> 00:42:04.660
said the ant. Well then, why don't you keep on playing and dancing now through the winter?

00:42:05.270 --> 00:42:12.420
I can't give you any food. The cricket was very sad that the ant wouldn't give her food. She didn't

00:42:12.420 --> 00:42:21.240
know who she could turn to, and she was hungry and cold. But even though it was cold, she began

00:42:21.240 --> 00:42:28.160
to play her fiddle and dance about, but she only played very softly, and only for herself. She

00:42:28.160 --> 00:42:29.960
loved music so much that while...

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:34.060
While playing her fiddle, she could almost forget how cold and hungry she was.

00:42:35.370 --> 00:42:39.810
It didn't take long before all the animals who had enjoyed listening to the cricket during the summer

00:42:39.810 --> 00:42:43.670
came out of their winter nests to listen to the cricket once again.

00:42:44.510 --> 00:42:48.820
They made a fire, they sang and danced, and were very happy.

00:42:49.440 --> 00:42:55.120
And the cricket was no longer hungry, for the animals had brought food with them for all to share.

00:42:57.390 --> 00:42:59.970
And she called to the aunt, too, to come to...

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:01.900
listen to the music with them all.
